    "tagline": "Illustrator & Graphic Designer | Hand-Drawn Art",
    "profile_description": "Hi, I’m Mahnoor A. I’m an illustrator and graphic designer, and I’ve been lucky enough to spend years doing what I genuinely love: drawing, designing, and bringing other people’s ideas to life.\n\nA big part of my work is children’s book illustration, character design, book covers, KDP projects, and illustration in general. I also work on logos, branding, banners, brochures, packaging, presentations, and other graphic design projects. I enjoy working closely with authors, businesses, publishers, and individuals and turning their ideas into something they can actually see, use, and be proud of.\n\nSome of the children’s books and illustrations I’ve worked on have been published, and my name has been credited in the books as the illustrator. I’ve also had my artwork featured on the cover of Cancer Cell, a highly respected scientific journal. Those are experiences I’m genuinely proud of because they remind me that the work I create can go much further than just a project being completed.\n\nI also want to be clear about something that is important to me: I don’t use AI to create my illustrations or designs. I’m an artist, and I still enjoy the process of actually creating the work myself. From the first sketch to the final details, I put my own time, ideas, and skills into what I deliver.\n\nI don’t believe every project needs to be complicated. Sometimes a client has a complete vision, and sometimes they only have a rough idea and need someone to help shape it. Either way, I’m happy to listen, discuss the details, and figure out the best way to bring it together.\n\nIf you have a project in mind, I’d love to hear about it. Maybe we can create something great together.",
